# Check the table schema before designing UI

Before adding, keeping, or restyling a form, profile, or any screen that reads or saves records, inspect the real table columns. Do this before writing the page.

- Read the live schema (`Schema::getColumnListing` or the database), not only the model `$fillable`, an old Blade form, or a UI mock.
- Every input name must match a column that exists, or a column you add in the same change.
- If the old form posts a field the table does not have, do not copy that field. Say which column is missing.
- A model relationship or fillable entry is not proof the column exists. Example: `users` had `country` (text) and no `country_id` or `title` until those columns were migrated.
